# The Glass Orchard
start: The Front Gate
theme: plain

// A garden-party mystery for about thirty guests. Mara Vell, who owns the
// orchard, has not been seen since the invitations went out. Her brother
// Ivo is hosting in her place and would rather nobody asked why.
//
// This is the spine of the project. The people live under `cast/`, the
// scenes under `beats/`, and the chat rooms in `rooms.loom`. It is written
// in the Loom 4 surface: names are words, instructions are plain verbs,
// and every reaction is a `when`.

// ── Groups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two sides a guest can take, and one they are not supposed to know about.

GROUP The Gardeners
  ethos: tend
  rival: The Collectors

GROUP The Collectors
  ethos: take
  rival: The Gardeners

GROUP The Society
  ethos: keep the orchard
  hidden: true

// ── Places ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

LOCATION Orchard Gate
  label: The Front Gate
  capacity: 40

LOCATION The Long Table
  label: The Long Table
  ambient: cutlery-and-crickets
  capacity: 40

LOCATION The Glasshouse
  label: The Glasshouse
  ambient: humid-hum
  capacity: 12

LOCATION The Cellar
  label: Under the Orchard
  ambient: drip
  capacity: 8

// ── Every guest ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The per-person state, plus the rules that apply to everyone.

ROLE Guest
  group: any of GROUP
  suspicion: 0 to 100 = 0
  favour: 0 to 100 = 10
  invited: bool = true
  below: bool = false

  // The one rule that can send a guest below: too much snooping, and the
  // Society quietly takes them down to the cellar.
  when self.suspicion >= 70:
    set self.below = true
    set self.suspicion = 0
    move self to The Cellar
    reply Someone takes your elbow. "This way. Mind the step."

  when arrives at The Cellar:
    broadcast lantern_low to participant(self)
    -> Under The Orchard

  when arrives at The Glasshouse:
    set self.suspicion += 5

  when joins The Gardeners:
    reply A sprig of rosemary is pinned to your lapel.

  when joins The Collectors:
    reply A small brass key is pressed into your palm.

  when someone joins:
    reply Welcome to the orchard. Keep your invitation where it can be scanned.

// ── What the app can do ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// Buttons the participant client offers, beyond scanning a pass. Each
// one is a named event: `when whisper for guest:` on a character hears
// the performer playing that character press it.

INTERACTION whisper
  label: Whisper to them
  who: performer
  description: A quiet word, in character, to one guest.

INTERACTION ring the bell
  label: Ring the bell
  who: guest
  description: The brass bell by the gate. Everyone hears it.

// ── House rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Story-level `when`s — they belong to nobody in particular.

when ring the bell for guest:
  broadcast "The bell by the gate rings. {guest.name} is standing under it." to location(Orchard Gate)
  set guest.suspicion += 5

when Tension > 80:
  fire the_toast
